<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 10 April, from 428 to 1998.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">428 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,598 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nestorius becomes Archbishop of Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nestorius was consecrated archbishop of the eastern capital. His teaching on the two natures of Christ was condemned at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ephesus">Ephesus</a> in 431, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-east">Church of the East</a> that kept his name spread as far as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-east">Church of the East</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1606">1606 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">420 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James I charters the Virginia Company</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King James I granted a charter to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a> Company's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> and Plymouth branches to settle the North American coast. The London company founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a> the following year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1710">1710 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">316 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Statute of Anne, the first copyright law, takes effect</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s Statute of Anne came into force, vesting copyright in authors rather than printers for a term of 14 years, renewable once. It set the principle on which modern copyright law is built.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1815">1815 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mount Tambora reaches its cataclysmic climax</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Indonesian volcano produced the largest eruption in recorded history, killing tens of thousands on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumbawa">Sumbawa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombok">Lombok</a>. Its ash cooled the globe, making 1816 the 'Year Without a Summer'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1912">1912 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Titanic leaves Southampton on her maiden voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">RMS Titanic, the largest ship afloat, sailed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southampton">Southampton</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> via Cherbourg and Queenstown. Five days later she struck an iceberg and sank with the loss of more than 1,500 lives.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1998">1998 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">28 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Good Friday Agreement is signed in Belfast</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The British and Irish governments and most Northern Ireland parties agreed a settlement creating a power-sharing assembly and cross-border bodies. It largely brought three decades of the Troubles to a close.</p></div></li></ol>
